---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { calendarUrl, whatsappUrl } from '../../../i18n/contact';
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  routeKey="about"
  canonicalPath="/en/about/"
  title="About | Product, design and software engineering | Next Wrld"
  description="Meet Next Wrld, our team, experience and way of thinking about products, systems and software solutions for companies."
>
  <section class="hero" data-od-id="hero">
    <div class="wrap" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Next Wrld</p>
      <h1>We build technology with business judgment.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Next Wrld starts from one idea: before building software you need to understand which problem is worth solving.</p>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">We combine product, design and engineering to create solutions that are useful for the business and for the people who will use them.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-p" href="/en/case-studies/" data-od-id="hero-primary">See our work</a>
        <a class="btn btn-s" href="/en/how-we-work/" data-od-id="hero-secondary">How we work</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band" data-od-id="por-que-existimos">
    <div class="wrap" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Why we exist</p>
      <h2>Software should simplify work.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Many companies grow by accumulating tools, spreadsheets, manual processes and systems that work separately.</p>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">What used to be enough can start requiring more coordination, more repetitive tasks and more people moving information from one place to another.</p>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">We start by understanding what is happening, what you want to improve and which path is worth following, before talking about software.</p>
      <p class="support">We understand before building, we connect business and technology, and we keep things simple when possible.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band" data-od-id="equipo" style="border-top:0">
    <div class="wrap" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">The team</p>
      <h2>A team with different disciplines on the same problem.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Next Wrld brings together product, design and engineering profiles to build end-to-end solutions.</p>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">Depending on each project, we combine experience in product, UI/UX, frontend, backend, architecture, automation, integrations and infrastructure.</p>
      <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">Gabriel Pérez Federico and Cleibert Castillo lead Next Wrld and are the visible faces of the company, but we work with a broader team.</p>
      <p class="statement">We want each person to contribute where they can add value, without adding unnecessary layers between the problem and the people solving it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section data-od-id="liderazgo">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who leads Next Wrld</p>
        <h2>We lead from two perspectives on the same product.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Gabriel and Cleibert lead Next Wrld’s direction from two different places.</p>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">Product, experience and engineering are part of the same conversation from the start.</p>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal>
        <div class="founder first">
          <span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">GP</span>
          <div><h3>Gabriel Pérez Federico</h3><span class="role">CO-FOUNDER · PRODUCT &amp; ENGINEERING</span><p>Gabriel works across product, engineering and software architecture, turning business needs into systems that sustain real processes.</p><p>His experience combines two different contexts: developing and evolving software inside established organizations, and building products from their earliest decisions.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Product and engineering experience</p>
        <div class="tags"><span>backend development</span><span>software architecture</span><span>distributed systems</span><span>management platforms</span><span>automation</span><span>integrations</span><span>messaging</span><span>infrastructure</span><span>data modeling</span><span>evolving existing products</span><span>building products from scratch</span></div>
        <h4>Global Hitss</h4>
        <span class="where">BACKEND · INTEGRATIONS · DIGITAL CONTENT</span>
        <p>He worked on backend systems and integrations for digital content processing and distribution.</p>
        <p>His work has included asynchronous processing, messaging, databases, automation and integrations tied to content flows for platforms such as Disney+, Prime Video and Apple TV.</p>
        <h4>Telecentro</h4>
        <span class="where">BACKEND · MICROSERVICES · TELECOMMUNICATIONS</span>
        <p>He developed backend services, integrations and event-driven processes for telecommunications and digital services.</p>
        <p>He has worked with Go microservices, Kafka-based processing, MongoDB and integrations with external providers, in systems where reliability, traceability and idempotency are an important part of the design.</p>
        <h4>JFHP</h4>
        <span class="where">LONG-TERM PRODUCT OWNERSHIP</span>
        <p>For several years, Gabriel has been directly involved in evolving a platform used by an international organization.</p>
        <p>His work has included legacy modernization, redesign of parts of the data model, backend and frontend evolution, architecture, new features, deployment and ongoing maintenance.</p>
        <p>The platform centralizes areas such as users, teams, locations, reporting, training, inventory and different access levels.</p>
        <p>Gabriel works directly with the person responsible for the product, taking part in both technical decisions and needs and priority definition.</p>
        <p class="scale">The platform has around 14,000 registered accounts, as context for the scale the system sustains.</p>
        <h4>Venfast</h4>
        <span class="where">PREVIOUS EXPERIENCE AS CO-FOUNDER</span>
        <p>Before Next Wrld, Gabriel also co-founded Venfast, working on service architecture, APIs and product building.</p>
        <p>That experience reinforced a way of working where product and engineering are thought together from the start.</p>
        <h4>Next Wrld · Own products</h4>
        <span class="where">AION WELLNESS · INMOCRM</span>
        <p>At Next Wrld, that experience converges in own products such as AION Wellness and InmoCRM and in projects where he takes part from understanding the problem to defining product, architecture, data, backend, integrations and infrastructure.</p>
        <p class="statement">His work is deciding which system makes sense to build, as well as how to build it.</p>
      </div>
      <div data-reveal>
        <div class="founder" style="margin-top:56px">
          <span class="mark" aria-hidden="true">CC</span>
          <div><h3>Cleibert Castillo</h3><span class="role">CO-FOUNDER · PRODUCT EXPERIENCE &amp; FRONTEND</span><p>Cleibert works at the intersection of user experience and frontend development, turning business needs into clear, easy-to-use interfaces.</p><p>He works with Vue.js and React, UI/UX design, prototyping, e-commerce and digital payments, always tied to commercial goals.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="bg" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Product and experience background</p>
        <h4>Next Wrld</h4>
        <span class="where">FRONTEND · PRODUCT EXPERIENCE</span>
        <p>At Next Wrld he focuses especially on product experience, interface design and frontend development of solutions such as AION Wellness and InmoCRM.</p>
        <p>He has also taken part in developing the brand’s own digital experience.</p>
        <h4>Imperium Business</h4>
        <span class="where">DIGITAL EXPERIENCES · COMMERCE AND PAYMENTS</span>
        <p>He developed digital platforms, landing pages and commerce and payment flows.</p>
        <p>He has worked with WordPress, Stripe, WooPayments and conversion-oriented experiences.</p>
        <h4>Tour App</h4>
        <span class="where">UI/UX · PROTOTYPING</span>
        <p>He designed wireframes, interactive prototypes and usability tests, and carried UI/UX decisions into product with engineering teams.</p>
        <p class="statement">His focus is turning product logic into a clear experience for the people who have to use it every day.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band" data-od-id="direccion-complementaria">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Two perspectives, one direction</p>
        <h2>We care about what happens behind the system as much as what the user experiences.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Neither the interface nor the architecture is enough on its own.</p>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">You need to understand the problem, define the product, design a clear experience and build a technical base that sustains it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="duo" data-reveal>
        <span class="lvl">NEXT WRLD</span>
        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
        <div class="names"><span>Gabriel</span><i>↔</i><span>Cleibert</span></div>
        <span class="co">PRODUCT &amp; ENGINEERING&nbsp;&nbsp;↔&nbsp;&nbsp;PRODUCT EXPERIENCE</span>
        <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</span>
        <span class="lvl">TEAM</span>
        <div class="teamline">Product · Design · Engineering</div>
      </div>
      <div class="grid2" data-reveal>
        <div class="cell cell-accent"><h3>Gabriel · Product &amp; Engineering</h3><div class="tags"><span>product definition</span><span>architecture</span><span>backend</span><span>APIs and integrations</span><span>distributed systems</span><span>automation</span><span>data</span><span>infrastructure</span><span>technical evolution</span></div></div>
        <div class="cell cell-accent"><h3>Cleibert · Product Experience &amp; Frontend</h3><div class="tags"><span>product experience</span><span>UI/UX</span><span>frontend</span><span>interfaces</span><span>prototyping</span><span>e-commerce</span><span>payments</span><span>usability</span><span>conversion</span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="cell" data-reveal style="margin-top:48px;border-top-color:var(--accent)"><h3>Next Wrld Team</h3><p style="color:var(--muted);max-width:64ch">Each project combines these perspectives with design, frontend, backend, product and infrastructure as needed. Gabriel and Cleibert lead direction and important decisions.</p><div class="tags"><span>design</span><span>frontend</span><span>backend</span><span>product</span><span>infrastructure</span><span>other disciplines per project</span></div></div>
      <p class="duo-close" data-reveal>Gabriel, Cleibert and the rest of the team think of each solution as a complete product.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section data-od-id="relacion-directa">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">A direct relationship</p>
        <h2>Close to the problem and the decisions.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Gabriel and Cleibert remain directly involved in Next Wrld’s direction and in important product and technology decisions.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid2" data-reveal>
        <div class="cell"><h3>Shared context</h3><p>We seek to understand why a problem exists before proposing how to solve it.</p></div>
        <div class="cell"><h3>Direct communication</h3><p>You discuss important decisions with the people defining the solution.</p></div>
        <div class="cell"><h3>Explained decisions</h3><p>We explain what we are doing, which alternatives exist and why we recommend a path.</p></div>
        <div class="cell"><h3>Responsibility</h3><p>We stay involved from understanding the problem until the solution can be used in a real context.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="statement" data-reveal>Tell us what is happening and what you want to improve, without technical terms.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band" data-od-id="experiencia-empresa">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Applied experience</p>
        <h2>We have worked on systems that already have to run, and built products from scratch.</h2>
        <p class="lead">We evolve existing software and build products from an idea.</p>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">We look at each project from three places: business, user and system.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="exp-list" data-reveal>
        <li>digital products built from scratch;</li>
        <li>management systems;</li>
        <li>platforms used by real organizations;</li>
        <li>existing software modernization;</li>
        <li>legacy system migration;</li>
        <li>backend and architecture;</li>
        <li>frontend and UI/UX;</li>
        <li>process automation;</li>
        <li>integrations between tools;</li>
        <li>event-driven systems;</li>
        <li>e-commerce and payments;</li>
        <li>infrastructure and deployment;</li>
        <li>continuous product evolution.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section data-od-id="productos-propios">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">Own products</p>
        <h2>We face our own product decisions.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Building our own products forces us to ask the same questions that appear in our clients’ projects.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="aion" data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">A product by Next Wrld</p>
        <h3>AION Wellness</h3>
        <span class="tag">PLATFORM · FITNESS CENTERS</span>
        <p>Platform for fitness centers designed to centralize memberships, plans, payments, members and cash closes in the same experience.</p>
        <div class="q"><p>We decide what is worth building, what stays out and how to validate each decision.</p></div>
        <p>AION lets us live the product from both sides: as the team that designs and develops, and as the people responsible for deciding what to build and how to evolve it.</p>
        <a class="cta" href="https://www.aionwellness.pro/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Meet AION Wellness →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="inmo" data-reveal>
        <span class="who">INMOCRM · PROPTECH</span>
        <h3>InmoCRM</h3>
        <p>PropTech product developed as an MVP around real estate processes. MVP developed, not yet implemented in a real company.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section data-od-id="lo-que-no-somos">
    <div class="wrap mini-statement" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow" style="justify-content:center">What we don’t want to be</p>
      <p class="anti">We are not a feature factory.</p>
      <p>Part of our work is deciding what is not worth building.</p>
      <p class="nos">We don’t confuse feature quantity with product quality.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="band" data-od-id="nuestra-forma">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div data-reveal>
        <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
        <h2>Understand, decide, build, put into use and improve.</h2>
        <p class="lead">We treat product, design and engineering in the same conversation.</p>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top:12px">First we understand what is happening and decide the path. Then we build the solution, bring it into the real context and evolve it as needs change.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="link-arrow" href="/en/how-we-work/" data-reveal>See how we work →</a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="final" data-od-id="cta-final">
    <div class="wrap" data-reveal>
      <p class="eyebrow">Let’s work together</p>
      <h2>Let’s talk with the people who will decide.</h2>
      <p>If there is a process, system or way of working starting to limit your company, we can start by understanding what is happening.</p>
      <p style="margin-top:12px">Then we define together which path is worth following.</p>
      <div class="cta-row"><a class="btn btn-w" href={calendarUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-od-id="final-primary">Analyze my case</a><a class="btn btn-g" href={whatsappUrl('en', 'full')} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Chat on WhatsApp</a></div>
      <p class="micro">Free initial diagnostic · 30–45 minutes</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  h1 { font-size: clamp(36px, 5vw, 64px); margin: 22px 0 20px; }
  h2 { font-size: clamp(28px, 3.4vw, 46px); margin: 18px 0; }
  section { padding: 96px 0; scroll-margin-top: 80px; }
  .hero { padding: 84px 0 88px; }
  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 14px; margin-top: 30px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .btn-p:hover { background: #1f49b4; transform: translateY(-1px); box-shadow: 0 12px 28px rgba(10, 78, 220, 0.35); }
  .btn-s:hover { border-color: var(--accent); background: #dce6ff; }
  .btn-w { background: #fff; color: var(--accent); }
  .btn-w:hover { background: #dce6ff; }
  .btn-g { border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.45); color: #fff; }
  .btn-g:hover { border-color: #fff; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); }
  .band { background: var(--surface-gray); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .statement { margin-top: 28px; font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 30px); max-width: 36ch; line-height: 1.3; }
  .support { margin-top: 16px; font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); max-width: 64ch; }
  .grid2 { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 48px 64px; margin-top: 56px; }
  .cell { border-top: 2px solid var(--fg); padding: 24px 0 0; }
  .cell-accent { border-top-color: var(--accent); }
  .cell h3 { font-family: var(--disp); font-size: 23px; margin-bottom: 8px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .cell p { color: var(--muted); max-width: 44ch; }
  .founder { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr; gap: 32px; padding: 40px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--fg); align-items: start; }
  .founder.first { margin-top: 48px; }
  .mark { width: 96px; height: 96px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--navy); color: #fff; display: grid; place-items: center; font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 700; font-size: 28px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; flex: none; }
  .founder .role { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--accent); display: block; margin: 8px 0 12px; }
  .founder h3 { font-family: var(--disp); font-size: clamp(24px, 2.8vw, 32px); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .founder p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 16px; max-width: 64ch; margin-top: 10px; }
  .bg { margin-top: 36px; }
  .bg .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .bg h4 { font-family: var(--disp); font-size: clamp(22px, 2.6vw, 30px); letter-spacing: -0.02em; margin: 26px 0 4px; }
  .bg h4:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }
  .bg .where { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--accent); display: block; margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .bg p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15.5px; max-width: 66ch; margin-top: 8px; }
  .bg p.scale { font-size: 13.5px; border-left: 2px solid var(--accent); padding-left: 14px; max-width: 60ch; }
  .tags { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin-top: 16px; }
  .tags span { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; padding: 6px 14px; color: var(--muted); background: var(--bg); }
  .duo { margin: 56px auto 0; max-width: 680px; text-align: center; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 20px; padding: 40px 32px; background: var(--surface); }
  .duo .lvl { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.2em; color: var(--muted); }
  .duo .co { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.2em; color: var(--accent); margin-top: 18px; display: block; }
  .duo .names { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; gap: 20px; margin: 14px 0; font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(22px, 3vw, 30px); }
  .duo .names i { font-style: normal; color: var(--accent); }
  .duo .arrow { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; font-size: 22px; display: block; margin: 6px 0; }
  .duo .teamline { margin-top: 14px; font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--muted); }
  .duo-close { margin-top: 32px; font-size: 17px; text-align: center; max-width: 60ch; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; }
  .exp-list { margin-top: 36px; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 16px; padding: 28px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 4px 32px; list-style: none; }
  .exp-list li { position: relative; font-size: 15.5px; padding: 8px 0 8px 26px; }
  .exp-list li::before { content: '·'; position: absolute; left: 4px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; font-size: 20px; line-height: 1.4; }
  .aion { background: var(--navy); color: #fff; border-radius: 22px; padding: clamp(30px, 4.5vw, 64px); margin-top: 48px; }
  .aion .eyebrow { color: #9dbcfb; }
  .aion .eyebrow::before { background: #9dbcfb; }
  .aion h3 { font-family: var(--disp); font-size: clamp(26px, 3.2vw, 40px); margin: 14px 0 6px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .aion .tag { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: #9dbcfb; }
  .aion p { color: #c9d4e8; max-width: 62ch; margin-top: 12px; }
  .aion .q { margin-top: 24px; border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2); padding-top: 20px; }
  .aion .q p { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: 20px; color: #fff; max-width: 52ch; }
  .aion a.cta { color: #fff; font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; display: inline-block; margin-top: 24px; text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #5e85e3; padding-bottom: 2px; }
  .inmo { margin-top: 20px; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 16px; padding: 24px 28px; background: var(--surface); }
  .inmo .who { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: 0.14em; color: var(--accent); }
  .inmo h3 { font-family: var(--disp); font-size: 22px; margin: 10px 0 6px; }
  .inmo p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; }
  .mini-statement { text-align: center; padding: 16px 0; }
  .mini-statement .anti { font-family: var(--serif); font-style: italic; font-size: clamp(26px, 3.4vw, 40px); letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  .mini-statement p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 15.5px; max-width: 56ch; margin: 16px auto 0; }
  .mini-statement .nos { margin-top: 20px; font-size: 15px; color: var(--muted); }
  .link-arrow { display: inline-block; margin-top: 24px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 16px; color: var(--fg); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); padding-bottom: 2px; }
  .final { background: var(--navy); color: #fff; text-align: center; padding: 130px 0; border-top: 4px solid #5e85e3; }
  .final .eyebrow { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.78); justify-content: center; }
  .final .eyebrow::before { background: #fff; }
  .final h2 { font-size: clamp(34px, 4.4vw, 60px); max-width: 20ch; margin: 0 auto 18px; }
  .final p { color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.85); max-width: 52ch; margin: 0 auto; }
  .final .cta-row { justify-content: center; }
  .final .micro { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7); margin-top: 16px; }
  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    section { padding: 72px 0; }
    .hero .cta-row { flex-direction: column; align-items: stretch; }
    .hero .cta-row .btn { width: 100%; }
    .grid2 { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0; }
    .cell { padding-bottom: 36px; }
    .founder { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 18px; }
    .mark { width: 72px; height: 72px; font-size: 22px; }
    .exp-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .duo { padding: 32px 20px; }
    .duo .co { letter-spacing: 0.1em; overflow-wrap: break-word; }
    .final { padding: 88px 0; }
  }
</style>
